    "body": "Closes #54.\n\nCreates docs/learning/how-browsers-work.md, an Arabic guide explaining how a web browser works.\n\n## What it covers\n- Definition of a browser\n- The seven main stages (networking, HTML parsing, CSS parsing, JavaScript execution, layout, paint, compositing)\n- A reference to the corresponding source directory for each stage\n- A suggested reading path for new contributors\n- Authoritative sources and project cross-references\n\n## Purpose\nThis guide, together with url-format.md, completes the docs/learning/ directory, giving new contributors the theoretical background they need before reading the code.\n\n## Also\n- Adds a link from docs/architecture.md (Further Reading section)\n- Adds a cross-link from docs/learning/url-format.md",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-28T05:08:35Z",
